ahh, the _irresistable_ lure of polypiles ...
let me say that polypiling is _guaranteed_ to work (if used properly, the
polymorph reaction is unstable and breeds more wands).  you will have stats
like 18/** 24 18 24 24 24 if you want!  AC -40, no problem.  max
experience, got it!  a couple of extra ALS for emergencies, is a dozen
enough? and so on.  its fun (and legitimate) but it's not how the game
was intended to be played.  keep that in mind.

[] limit to the amount of stuff that can be on one level at a time? How

limited only by available memory.  objects are kept in a dynamically
allocated linked list.  i personally have polypiled, at once, over 800
items (VAX/Unix).  however 250 item piles are far more the norm.
btw, by pile i mean 3 stashes with about 80 items in a stash all in
a line adjacent to each other.

[] about the amount that can be on one pile at a time? And what is the range
[] of a wand of polymorph, i.e. how many piles can I line up and poly with
[] one zap?

you can only count on a range of 3 squares.  you may get an extended
range upto 6 squares (i think) but you cannot count on it.  professional
polypilers always sort the piles according to some preferred strategy
(perhaps by blessing status or perhaps by object classes, etc.).

the only drawback, if you win you'll have this feeling that it was
too easy ...

